window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>He took me captive. Now I own his black heart.</b><br> <br> Damian Cross, the most feared man at Ashford University, claimed me as his latest sacrifice.<br> <br> There is no escape for a good girl like me. Not from the wealthy heir to Ashford’s most elite secret society–The Four Hundred.<br> <br> \"You’re mine now,\" he vows, his touch searing through every wall I try to build. \"And I’ll destroy anyone who dares to touch what belongs to me.\"<br> <br> I’m a pastor’s daughter who’s spent her life following every rule. Good. Pure. Perfect.<br> <br> He’s the ruthless prince who bends the world to his will. Cruel. Cunning. Dark.<br> <br> I should hate him. But there’s something in the way he watches me—like I’m the only thing holding him together—that shatters every defense I have.<br> <br> When love is born in darkness, it doesn’t just burn. It consumes.<br> <br> He may be a prince, but I have all the power.</p>"; 
